<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria to offer 25 bln levs 89-day T-bills Dec30.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria to offer 25 bln levs 89-day T-bills Dec30.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry will offer 25 billion levs of 89-day floater coupon T-bills at an auction on Monday, the central bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue will be offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry.</p>
<p>The coupon equals the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at 15 percent monthly or 180 percent annually.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow:</p>
<p> Issue number	 BG 3010097023</p>
<p> Auction date	 December 30, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date	   January 3, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date	April 2, 1997</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
